### A.1 What is MAD 2? — The Big Picture
**[0:19 – 1:55]**

**What it is:**
MAD 2 (Modern Application Development 2) is the sequel to MAD 1. Where MAD 1 taught you to build a full application using **Flask (Python) + basic HTML/CSS/a little JS**, MAD 2 goes deeper — introducing a **real front-end framework (Vue.js)** and **advanced backend concepts** (security, async jobs, caching).

**Why it exists (intuition):**
In MAD 1, your web pages were mostly rendered by the server (Flask renders HTML and sends it to the browser). This works, but it's limited — modern apps (Gmail, Instagram, Google Maps) don't reload the whole page every time you click something. MAD 2 exists to teach you *how* professional apps achieve that interactivity, and how to secure and scale a backend once your app becomes "real."

